{
  "about": "Shared views for the ocean comparison rig (tools/nature/compare.mjs). One camera, sun and sea state per view; compare.mjs renders Ultra-Water (three.js, run locally from E:\\ref\\ultra-water) and our spectral sea from the same numbers. World frame: y up; headings in degrees with 0 = +x and 90 = +z (our convention; compare.mjs converts the sun to Ultra-Water's azimuth, 90 - heading). camera.eye in metres, camera.yaw_deg the heading looked along, camera.pitch_deg negative looks down, camera.fov_deg vertical. Ultra-Water sits the camera far out at sea (away from its island) for open-water views; a view with a 'shore' block is placed on its coast (see compare.mjs). 'ours.preset' is the Ocean item's preset in catalog/procedural/procedural.json (its base first), 'ours.set' overrides material.nature.* values; 'ultra_water.*' are values on window.app objects of the Ultra-Water page (waves: ocean.params, sky: sky.params, water: the Water panel's values, post: post.params).",
